****
Magnesium and Sodium are really odd balls of the spectrum. They show obvious prominences, bright plages, and very dens filaments do show up. 
Overall, both the Na I D and the Mg I b disk is an anemic variant of a broad band selection of the Ca II K/H region.

While at this green magnesium, let's mention that there is an ultraviolet Mg triplet, showing similar features, 
with relatively bright prominences, at around lambda 3838. 

It was the prominence showing up at the UV sibling of this Magnesium that made me dig deep into spectroheliography, 
to look into the literature, and identify the lines myself.
